        "x-amazon-apigateway-integration": {
          "type": "aws_proxy",
          "credentials": {
            "Fn::Sub": "${ApiRole.Arn}"
          },
          "uri": {
            "Fn::Sub": "arn:aws:apigateway:${AWS::Region}:lambda:path/2015-03-31/functions/${uploadFilesForJob.Arn}/invocations"
          },
          "passthroughBehavior": "never",
          "httpMethod": "POST",
          "connectionType": "INTERNET",
          "contentHandling": "CONVERT_TO_TEXT"
        },
        "x-amazon-apigateway-request-validator": "all",
        "security": [
          {
            "DdamenLambdaAuthorizer": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Upload Video Files to Our Servers for AI Analysis",
        "description": "Upload Video Files to Our Servers for AI Analysis",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "x-api-key",
            "description": "API Key provided to you by 2 Minute Warning. The API Key is used to identify \n    the Third Party client making the request. Please keep this key secure.<br><br>\n    <strong>Note: </strong>Make sure that the key <code>x-api-key</code> are all small caps.",
            "in": "header",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^[a-zA-Z0-9]+$",
              "minLength": 3,
              "maxLength": 256,
              "example": "1234567890abcdef"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "x-user-token",
            "description": "The word <code>Bearer</code> followed by the <code>idToken</code>\n    you received from the <code>/login</code> endpoint. It is a\n    long string and is used to authenticate and identify users making the api request.<br><br>\n    <strong>Notes: </strong><br>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Make sure that the key <code>x-user-token</code> are all small caps.</li>\n      <li>Make sure the word <code>Bearer</code> precedes the <code>idToken</code>, separated by a space.</li>\n      <li>If the token is expired, you can get a new <code>idToken</code> from the\n        <code>/refreshToken</code> endpoint.</li>\n    </ul>",
            "in": "header",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^Bearers[A-Za-z0-9-_=]+.[A-Za-z0-9-_=]+.?[A-Za-z0-9-_.+/=]*$",
              "minLength": 3,
              "maxLength": 4096,
              "example": "Bearer eyJraWQiOiJSVVdxd3l..."
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "videoClips"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "jobID": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "example": "00085"
                  },
                  "videoClips": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "minItems": 1,
                    "items": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "required": [
                        "cameraView",
                        "filename"
                      ],
                      "properties": {
                        "cameraView": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "enum": [
                            "SL",
                            "EZ",
                            "SB"
                          ],
                          "example": "SL"
                        },
                        "filename": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9 \\-_.&,]+\\.mp4$",
                          "minLength": 5,
                          "maxLength": 256,
                          "example": "Uni-A-vs-Uni-B-Play-008.mp4"
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "description": "<style>\n    /* This is for local purposes only. Swagger removes these styles on the Web UI. */\n    code {\n        color: pink;\n        font-weight: bold;\n    }\n</style>\n\n<h3>Uploading Video Clips for Analysis</h3>\n\n<p><code>Note: </code>If your videos clips are hosted in the cloud and a direct link to the video is available, you do not need to use this endpoint.</p>\n\n<p>This endpoint returns secured URLs where you can use to upload video clips to our servers, prior to requesting for AI analysis. This endpoint is available for video clips stored in your computer and not through direct links.</p>\n\n<p>You will also receive the S3 paths to use for each clip when submitting a new job. Instead of <code>https://</code> links, use these returned S3 file paths, and our servers will look into the storage where you would have uploaded the video clips.</p>\n\n<p>You may optionally enter a <code>jobID</code>, and the returned upload URLs will place your video clips to the respective job ID. If you do not specify a <code>jobID</code>, we will create one for you.</p>\n\n\n<h3>Return Payload:</h3>\n\n<ul>\n    <li><code>clientID</code>: the client id associated with your client.</li>\n    <li><code>jobID</code>: the job ID to where the video clips will be placed. Use this <code>jobID</code> when making a job request for the uploaded video clips.</li>\n    <li>\n        <code>uploadURLs</code>: a list of parameters for your submitted filenames:\n        <ul>\n            <li><code>filename</code>: the filename of the video clip</li>\n            <li><code>s3Location</code>: the S3 location where the video clip will be stored</li>\n            <li><code>uploadUrl</code>: the secured URL to call when uploading the video clip</li>\n        </ul>\n    </li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h3>How to Use the Returned Upload URL</h3>\n\n<p>The secured upload URLs require a <code>PUT</code> method request with the binary data of the video clip. Below are examples in <code>Python</code> and <code>Javascript</code>.</p>\n\n<h3>Python Example</h3>\n<pre>\n    <code>\n\n        # This script requires the \"requests\" package: pip install requests\n        import requests\n\n        # You can get the user token by logging in (see /login endpoint)\n        uploadURL = \"https://apis.2minutewarning.com/v1/uploadFilesForJob\"\n        xUserToken = \"eyJraWQiOiJSVVdx . . .\"\n        xApiKey = \"abcdefg123456 . . .\"\n\n        def main():\n\n            # Prepare the request body payload\n            body = {\n                \"jobID\": \"00085\", # optionally specify the jobID\n                \"videoClips\": [\n                    {\n                        \"cameraView\": \"SL\",\n                        \"filename\": \"LHS-vs-Enumclaw-11-26-2022-Play-013.mp4\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"cameraView\": \"SL\",\n                        \"filename\": \"LHS-vs-Enumclaw-11-26-2022-Play-014.mp4\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"cameraView\": \"SL\",\n                        \"filename\": \"LHS-vs-Enumclaw-11-26-2022-Play-015.mp4\"\n                    }\n                ]\n            }\n\n            # User token and API Key\n            headers = {\n                \"X-User-Token\": f\"Bearer {xUserToken}\",\n                \"X-Api-Key\": xApiKey,\n            }\n            \n            # Send HTTP Request with the payload and headers\n            response = requests.post(uploadURL, json=body, headers=headers)\n\n            # Get the json response\n            jsonObj = response.json()\n\n            # Extract the data from the response\n            data = jsonObj[\"data\"]\n\n            # Get the array of uploadUrls\n            uploadUrls = data[\"uploadUrls\"]\n\n            for uploadUrl in uploadUrls:\n                # Get the filename for this video clip\n                # We will need this to make sure we use the correct\n                # video clip when uploading the file\n                filename = uploadUrl[\"filename\"]\n\n                # Get the uploadUrl\n                uploadUrl = uploadUrl[\"uploadUrl\"]\n\n                # Read the file and upload it to the uploadUrl\n                with open(filename, 'rb') as file:\n                    response = requests.put(uploadUrl, data=file)\n                    print(f\"Uploaded {filename} with status code {response.status_code}\")\n\n\n            # Print end of script\n            print(\"Finished uploading all video clips!\")\n                \n\n        if __name__ == '__main__':\n            main()\n\n    </code>\n</pre>"
        }
      }
    },
